If a patient has a renal-insufficiency and a clinician prescribes an opioid to the patient then the clinician should prescribe the opioid cautiously to the patient and should increase a patient-monitoring for the patient and should minimize an opioid-risk for the patient.
If a patient has a hepatic-insufficiency and a clinician prescribes an opioid to the patient then the clinician should prescribe the opioid cautiously to the patient and should increase a patient-monitoring for the patient and should minimize an opioid-risk for the patient.
If a patient has an age and the age includes at least 65 years and a clinician prescribes an opioid to the patient then the clinician should prescribe the opioid cautiously to the patient and should increase a patient-monitoring for the patient and should minimize an opioid-risk for the patient.
